            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GREENFIREFLY"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Half the sugar as previously advised was plenty. The apples were ok, but the egg white was just more of the same texture. It needs something oaty or crunchy or something. Since raw egg whites scare me anyway I won't make it again.",
            "datePublished": "2007-08-02T17:41:37.487Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "busymama"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really nicely spiced. I cut the sugar down to 1/2 cup and thought it was still too sweet, so I think I'll cut sugar down to 1/4 cup next time. No need for egg white or meringue powder - it's great without it. Delicious straight up or as a topping.",
            "datePublished": "2006-11-12T17:39:07.000Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jaime"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is great! You can also make it with just original, premade applesauce and skip the sugar. So delicious, I made it twice in the past 2 days!",
            "datePublished": "2006-03-11T18:20:23.560Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
